+
+## 21. Prospective Validation Storage / Operational V2 (2026-10-20)
+
+**Behavior change: YES. Existing strategy behavior changed: NO.** This is an
+operational/storage protocol, not Strategy V2 or another research campaign.
+V1's full immutable snapshots multiply files by symbol × arm × run. V2 retains
+the same scientific inputs and computation, publishing only new observations
+in long tables. No new dependency, strategy predicate, execution loop, lifecycle
+formula, candidate, metric or cost calculation is introduced.
+
+### Preserved V1 and new freeze
+
+`results/prospective_validation/PV-V1-20261020/` remains byte-for-byte unchanged,
+including its hashes and offline evidence. It is an immutable infrastructure
+proof with no real validation observations. Its reproduction commit is
+`4ddd33c050273fec587e1172adffae4d6b1bd188`. Even adding source modules changes
+V1's glob-based source identity, so reproduce V1 at that original commit; do
+not rewrite its freeze to accept V2.
+
+`src/live_scanner_v2.py` owns the distinct `PV-V2-20261020` protocol.
+Initialization verifies and copies V1's exact universe, candidates and original
+seed. Baseline settings, four reference policies, ten shadow candidates, metrics,
+costs, exclusion rules and old cutoff are inherited verbatim. Existing V1 source
+hashes must still match. V2 records current HEAD, working-tree diff/status,
+all current source hashes, runtime, actual freeze timestamp and storage schemas.
+The timestamp is finalized after an old-seed-only schema probe and before atomic
+publication. No provider call is possible through initialization. The full seed
+is copied once, not into daily partitions.
+
+The old snapshot remains strictly before 2026-09-22. The authoritative V2
+prospective boundary is its own `frozen_at`, not V1's. Availability and evidence
+classification reuse V1 unchanged: Daily completion after 16:15 New York;
+pre-freeze availability is `TEMPORAL_OOS_LATER_UNSEEN`; a scan's latest completed
+bar is `PROSPECTIVE_PAPER` only on a date strictly after the V2 freeze's NY date
+and before next calendar day 09:30 NY. Other post-freeze bars remain
+`POST_FREEZE_BACKFILL_NOT_PROSPECTIVE`, unable to originate eligible trades.
+First persisted classification never upgrades. Trade population follows signal
+origin even when its lifetime crosses the prospective boundary.
+
+### Source of truth and schemas
+
+The hierarchy is frozen protocol/seed → verified immutable events → derived
+mutable state/reports. The public Daily OHLCV index, timezone, full indicator
+warm-up, all 191 diagnostics, module masks and signal predicates remain unchanged.
+Five CSVs use `symbol`/`arm` columns; there are no published symbol/arm folders:
+
+| Table | Rows and availability |
+| --- | --- |
+| `bars.csv` | Only first-observed completed validation OHLCV, `timestamp`, `symbol`, `observed_at`, `available_at_utc`, evidence class |
+| `decisions.csv` | All 191 original diagnostic fields plus first-observation metadata, once per symbol/new bar, including no-signal bars; bar-close features only |
+| `signals.csv` | New eligible arm signals, mask/score, direction and provenance; eligible signals are not assertions of fills or scheduled orders |
+| `trade_events.csv` | Sparse typed union of `ENTRY_FILLED`, `EXIT_FILLED` and `EXECUTION_BAR`; copied from authoritative engine outputs |
+| `lifecycle_states.csv` | New survived-close `causal_path` observations: running return/MFE/MAE, strict high/stall, giveback/retention, age, ATR and stops |
+
+`ENTRY_FILLED` stores only entry-known fields, with next-observed-open
+availability; it never includes a future exit or final return. `EXIT_FILLED`
+stores the closed lifecycle record and frozen primary/stress accounting, marked
+as retrospective. Open exits are available at that open; intrabar stops and
+their excursion bounds are confirmed by the completed Daily bar, without an
+invented exact intrabar clock. `EXECUTION_BAR` copies the engine's active stop,
+next stop, stop-hit and trend-close flags. Next stops apply to the following
+bar. The trace does not invent a new explicit shadow pending-exit field.
+Pending entry/reconciliation and shadow pending-exit state remain reconstructible
+by the existing replay from frozen inputs. No terminal `CENSORED` event is
+invented for an ordinary daily prefix; mutable open trades retain V1's
+`closed=False`, `censored_at_end=True`, missing final returns.
+
+Signal keys are `session|symbol|arm|signal_time|direction`; trade keys use the
+same provenance. Event keys add type and event bar; state keys add `bar_time`.
+Bars/decisions use `(symbol, timestamp)`. The protocol hash in run metadata
+binds source/config identity for every row. `event_observed_at` and
+`event_available_at_utc` separate actual collection from model availability.
+First-observed states stay immutable even after a later trade closes.
+Operational trade snapshots retain V1's session-local key representation.
+
+`schemas.json` consolidates per-table columns, dtypes and exact object-string/
+None locations. Read event tables with `live_scanner_v2.read_table`, not a bare
+CSV inference. It preserves literal `NA`, empty strings, NaNs, nullable fields,
+float fidelity and timezones. Empty tables retain their frozen schema. V2
+explicitly types empty `research_signal_source` as object (V1's empty map inferred
+float); this is a storage representation correction, not a strategy change.
+
+### Layout, publication and recovery
+
+```text
+PV-V2-20261020/
+  freeze/                         immutable protocol, original seed and schemas
+  events/YYYY/MM/YYYY-MM-DD/NNNNNN/
+    run.json
+    bars.csv
+    decisions.csv
+    signals.csv
+    trade_events.csv
+    lifecycle_states.csv
+    schemas.json
+    completed.json                inventory/checksums and previous run hash
+  publication.jsonl               append-only publication receipts
+  state/
+    open_trades.csv
+    schemas.json
+    cursors.json
+    latest_run.json
+    completed.json
+  reports/latest/                 derived evaluation/distributions/report
+  failures/                       compact explicit attempt errors
+  verification/                   offline verification record
+```
+
+Date folders describe the invocation's NY date; row timestamps describe actual
+market sessions. Sequence suffixes permit explicit catch-up or a later new-bar
+run on the same date without overwriting evidence. A repeated input with no new
+completed bars publishes no partition, no duplicate signals, and no unrecorded
+as-of clock in state. The first historical-seed-only run also creates no event
+partition and remains `AWAITING_VALIDATION_DATA`.
+
+The CLI holds the existing process lock; library callers must hold
+`session_lock(base)` too. One atomic checksummed `.checkpoint.json` contains
+only each completed symbol's new evidence, open positions and observation clock.
+It does not contain full historical prices/diagnostics. Partial calculation is
+discarded; completed symbol checkpoints are retained and reused on `resume`,
+including their original clocks across dates. No partial universe can publish.
+A compact `.event-pending` directory is assembled, sealed, then atomically
+renamed. A verified orphan after rename is adopted; matching pending work is
+retired without another data fetch. Hash chains, sequence checks and the small
+publication receipt detect corrupt/missing evidence and a deleted published
+tail. Corrupt pending evidence fails closed.
+
+State is never a replay input. A corrupt, missing or stale state cache is
+reconstructed offline from the original seed and verified bars/decisions through
+the unchanged V1 computation. Closed evaluation records come from immutable
+exit events; only currently open trades are cached. `recover` rebuilds this
+cache explicitly. Evaluation overwrites `reports/latest` and still separates
+both eligible evidence classes, every baseline/reference/shadow arm and both
+cost scenarios, including zero-sample rows. No monthly snapshots are automatic.
+
+Each new-data run publishes **8 files**, independent of symbols/arms, plus an
+append to one publication receipt. State uses 5 files and latest reports use 5
+files, reused in place. At one run per 252 trading days this is approximately
+**2,016 new evidence files/year**, plus the one-time freeze, constant caches,
+verification and exceptional failures. A normal fully covered day has 50 bar
+rows, 50 diagnostic rows, 0–750 eligible signal rows, up to roughly 750 survived
+state rows and up to roughly 2,250 entry/exit/execution events across 50 × 15
+independent streams. Catch-up scales rows with newly observed bars, not file
+count. These maxima are structural bounds, not forecasts of signal frequency.
+
+### Operation and limits
+
+```sh
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m src.live_scanner_v2 init
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m src.live_scanner_v2 scan
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m src.live_scanner_v2 catch-up
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m src.live_scanner_v2 update
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m src.live_scanner_v2 resume
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m src.live_scanner_v2 recover
+PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 .venv/bin/python -m src.live_scanner_v2 report
+```
+
+`--session` selects a distinct frozen protocol; `--input-dir` uses local typed
+symbol CSVs behind the same verification gate. First real `scan` is deferred
+until review; implementation/freeze verification uses no post-snapshot market
+retrieval or inspection. Launchd, scheduling, alerts and subsequent research
+are outside this task.
+
+The storage adapter deliberately calls unchanged `PaperScanner._symbol` in
+temporary scratch, retaining full diagnostic and validation-stream replay CPU
+cost. This eliminates retained snapshot/file multiplication, not replay cost.
+Temporary computation is one symbol at a time and is removed afterward; an OS
+kill may leave temporary scratch for normal temp cleanup. Startup verifies the
+ledger and builds in-memory history, so time/memory still grow with history.
+No incremental indicator/execution engine or heavy storage dependency is added.
+
+V1's Daily/Long-only, exchange-calendar, next-observed-open, provider revision,
+fixed-universe, intrabar uncertainty, independent-stream and uncalibrated-cost
+limitations remain. Changed, duplicate, omitted or late-inserted observations
+fail closed. The provider's rolling five-year window eventually cannot supply
+all validation overlap; a reviewed retrieval extension will be needed before
+that boundary. Local hashes are corruption checks, not external notarization;
+deleting both the entire tail and its receipt cannot be detected from the
+remaining local history alone. No profitability or TradingView parity follows
+from offline engine equivalence.
